## Lore

The hawrk-ka are powerful, bird-like alien predators, sometimes mistaken for shedim demons or for Lone Star''s genetic creations. They come from the same world as the zembahk, and they prey on the zembahk, the hawrk-duhk and other smaller creatures. Their most important trait is that they are completely impervious to magic, a natural defense on a world dominated by mystic energy and magic-wielding creatures. The Splugorth trade on this and sell them as hunters, guards and protectors.

They are extremely aggressive, not very bright and hard to manage. They love to hunt and kill above all else, feeding on humanoids and on animals twice their size, and they fight fearlessly and without mercy, often to the death unless ordered otherwise, and sometimes have to be pulled off their prey even then. Unlike the duck-bills they are lone hunters who avoid their own kind except for mates or to fight. They respect the Splugorth and their minions. They never wear body armor, and most prefer their claws to weapons.

A male takes 1D4 females, who stay with him 2D6 years and sometimes for life. They mate every two years; a female lays 1D4 eggs that hatch in four months, and the young stay four more months until mature, when the male drives them off. There are three females for every male; the sexes are equally aggressive and about the same size, the females less colorful.

Alignment: any, but generally anarchist or evil. Weight 500 lbs (225 kg); typically 6 to 10 ft (1.8 to 3 m) tall. Typical NPCs are level 1D4. Average life span fifty years. Carnivores.

## GM Notes

Slave market value 100,000 to 300,000 credits. Sold in Atlantis and occasionally found in North America, Europe and Africa. Enemies: larger predators and humanoids. Tend to be loners but may work with groups.
